From 77d44bbd18abe05ca4105d015e7c7b1e5f861943 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 15:04:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] osx: use legacy-support's POSIX scandir() with the 10.6
 SDK

styles.c, iop/lut3d.c and iop/rasterfile.c pass scandir() a filter that
takes a const struct dirent *, the POSIX prototype, but the macOS 10.6
SDK still declares the filter without const and GCC rejects the call
under -Wincompatible-pointer-types. MacPorts legacy-support ships inline
wrappers with the POSIX signatures and substitutes them for scandir()
and alphasort() when _MACPORTS_LEGACY_COMPATIBLE_SCANDIR is defined
before <dirent.h> is first included.

Define it at the top of styles.c, which the library compiles directly,
and at the top of common/module_api.h for the two modules: they are
compiled with -include common/module_api.h, which brings in glib and
<dirent.h> before the first line of the module source, so a define in
the module itself would come too late. Anywhere else the macro is
unused.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017wUNQ69BaBcDfrxd6oXJeJ
---
 src/common/module_api.h | 8 ++++++++
 src/common/styles.c     | 6 ++++++
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git src/common/module_api.h src/common/module_api.h
--- src/common/module_api.h
+++ src/common/module_api.h
@@ -16,6 +16,14 @@
     along with darktable.  If not, see <http://www.gnu.org/licenses/>.
 */
 
+// ask MacPorts legacy-support for scandir() with the POSIX const filter
+// prototype, which the macOS 10.6 SDK lacks. modules get this header from
+// the command line ahead of their own first line, so for them this is the
+// only spot that precedes <dirent.h>
+#ifndef _MACPORTS_LEGACY_COMPATIBLE_SCANDIR
+#define _MACPORTS_LEGACY_COMPATIBLE_SCANDIR 1
+#endif
+
 #include <glib.h>
 
 #undef OPTIONAL
diff --git src/common/styles.c src/common/styles.c
--- src/common/styles.c
+++ src/common/styles.c
@@ -16,6 +16,12 @@
     along with darktable.  If not, see <http://www.gnu.org/licenses/>.
 */
 
+// ask MacPorts legacy-support for scandir() with the POSIX const filter
+// prototype, which the macOS 10.6 SDK lacks; must precede <dirent.h>
+#ifndef _MACPORTS_LEGACY_COMPATIBLE_SCANDIR
+#define _MACPORTS_LEGACY_COMPATIBLE_SCANDIR 1
+#endif
+
 #include "common/styles.h"
 #include "common/collection.h"
 #include "common/darktable.h"
